# LF in the repository, whatever the checkout does.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with `core.autocrlf=true` checks out CRLF,
# `.prettierrc` sets no `endOfLine`, and Prettier's `lf` default then flags the
# line endings of every file it looks at — 472 of them, none about formatting.
# The gate reads as broken and gets ignored, which is how a genuinely unwrapped
# line reaches CI.
#
# `text=auto` leaves git to detect text from binary, so images and archives are
# untouched. Fixing it here rather than with `endOfLine` in `.prettierrc` keeps
# CI enforcing LF for everyone instead of silencing the check per contributor.
* text=auto eol=lf
